From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:43:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ntfs: sync attribute inode size after resize

commit 3e38885ff66c797fc90cf90ab94c372bb4386e84 upstream.

Internal attribute truncation bypasses truncate_setsize(), so successful
resizes must update the attribute inode's i_size. Restrict the update to
attribute inodes to keep KEEP_SIZE fallocate from changing a file's i_size.

Fixes: 495e90fa3348 ("ntfs: update attrib operations")
Signed-off-by: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
---
 fs/ntfs/attrib.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/ntfs/attrib.c b/fs/ntfs/attrib.c
index 9c089839da15..2911cfab6147 100644
--- a/fs/ntfs/attrib.c
+++ b/fs/ntfs/attrib.c
@@ -5190,6 +5190,8 @@ int ntfs_attr_truncate_i_locked(struct ntfs_inode *ni, const s64 newsize,
 					ni, newsize, locked_ni, false);
 	} else
 		err = ntfs_resident_attr_resize(ni, newsize, 0, holes);
+	if (!err && NInoAttr(ni))
+		i_size_write(VFS_I(ni), newsize);
 	ntfs_debug("Return status %d\n", err);
 	return err;
 }
